SystemVerilog frontend
----------------------

pyslang 11.0.0 / Slang
  SPDX: MIT
  Project and source:
    https://github.com/MikePopoloski/slang
  Python package release:
    https://pypi.org/project/pyslang/11.0.0/
  Documentation:
    https://sv-lang.com/pyslang/
  License text in the installed wheel:
    pyslang-11.0.0.dist-info/licenses/LICENSE

HDL-X 0.2.0 declares pyslang only through the `systemverilog` optional extra
with an exact `==11.0.0` requirement. The HDL-X wheel does not bundle the
pyslang wheel or Slang binaries. Users who do not install this extra retain the
VHDL path; SystemVerilog requests fail explicitly at the frontend boundary.
The 0.2.0 CycloneDX SBOM includes the separately installed pyslang wheel
and the active-extra dependency relationship.

Primary VHDL runtime dependency
-------------------------------

pyGHDL 6.0.0 / libghdl
  SPDX: GPL-2.0-or-later
  Project and corresponding source:
    https://github.com/ghdl/ghdl/tree/v6.0.0
  Release and official platform wheels:
    https://github.com/ghdl/ghdl/releases/tag/v6.0.0
  License text in the official wheel:
    pyghdl-6.0.0.dist-info/licenses/COPYING.md

The official pyGHDL wheel is platform-specific and contains libghdl plus GHDL
standard/IEEE VHDL resources. It is not part of the HDL-X wheel or presented as
an HDL-X-owned release artifact.

